{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>YHWH, a man of war.</b> A master of wars — like ״אִישׁ נָעֳמִי״ (Ruth 1). And every אִישׁ and אִישֵׁךְ is rendered בַּעַל, and likewise ״וְחָזַקְתָּ וְהָיִיתָ לְאִישׁ״ (I Kings 2) — a mighty one." "<b>YHWH is His name.</b> His wars are not with weapons but in His name He wages war — as David said: ״וְאָנֹכִי בָא אֵלֶיךָ בְּשֵׁם YHWH צְבָאוֹת״ (I Samuel 17). Another interpretation: <b>YHWH is His name</b> — even at the time He wages war and takes vengeance on His enemies, He holds to His attribute of mercy for His creatures and sustains all who come into the world; not like the way of earthly kings — when one is occupied with war, he diverts himself from all other affairs and has no power to do both this and that (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:18.924640998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}